    "perplexity": {
      "description": "Dreadzone’s Second Light is the London collective’s acclaimed second album, originally released by Virgin in 1995. Subtitled An Original Dreadzone Sound Adventure, it is a boundary-crossing electronic record that combines dub, reggae, house, sampling, folk and Celtic influences into a distinctly multicultural British sound. Tracks such as “Life, Love And Unity,” “Zion Youth,” “Captain Dread” and “A Canterbury Tale” balance deep grooves with atmospheric textures, while “Little Britain” became the group’s biggest UK single.\n\nThe 2025 Record Store Day edition presents the album as a 2LP pressing on orange and blue vinyl through Universal Music Recordings/Virgin, marking its 30th anniversary. It includes a revised vocal version of “Little Britain”—the form Dreadzone have long performed live—in place of the instrumental version found on the original release. A defining and most commercially successful Dreadzone album, Second Light remains notable for its adventurous fusion of club music, roots culture and live-band energy.",
